@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/terrace#> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/orexis/reporting#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .

#  This agent's PRIVATE beliefs — one block, because it composed one capability.
#
#  No region want, so no opinion about what a reading MEANS: no aim, no band, no price. No review
#  interval, because world.ttl grants no mandate. And no interval to ask a board for: this
#  agent LISTENS to a sentinel that keeps its own clock, so sensing:fastSleepS, slowSleepS and
#  alarmDeltaFraction would be theatre, and the listening shape forbids them.

##  sensing:Listening — how stale a heartbeat may be before it stops trusting it
#
#  An ABSOLUTE, and the one figure that sets the board's battery life: render_sentinel fits
#  the heartbeat under it as max(60, 0.8 * this), so 300 s here compiles a 240 s heartbeat —
#  around 360 wakes a day, roughly the sentinel README's governed-node row rather than its
#  four-month one. Chosen SHORT for bring-up, deliberately: a node whose working has not been
#  seen wants to be heard often. Raise it to 1800 or 3600 once the lamp has said so, and
#  regenerate: the heartbeat follows this belief and nothing else.
:terrace_agent
    sensing:maxReadingAgeS 1500 ;
    sensing:readingGraceS 120 .        # every perceiver states one; the slack past a
                                       # heartbeat before a reading counts as old

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
:terrace_agent reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .
